@title STORY • ALANA: 10K PACE
@bg dorm_room_morning
You're Alana Brooks. 5:30 a.m. Your alarm, your backup alarm, and your backup-backup alarm all go off at once. Cassie throws a pillow at all three.
Cassie: Some of us dream, Alana.
Alana: Some of us PR.
Your planner is open on the desk. Every hour color-coded. Blue for training. Green for class. There is no color for "fun." You never needed one.
Your phone buzzes. Cam Hayes: "eastbrook's indoor track has better lights. just saying."
> [Bold] "your splits don't." -> a1
> [Sweet] Smile at your phone. Don't answer yet. -> a2
> [Good] Mute him. You have intervals. -> a3
*a1
@add Alana_Cam 2
Cam: "ouch. accurate. coffee after your meet saturday?"
You stare at "coffee" for longer than it takes to run 400 meters.
@jump a_done
*a2
@add Alana_Cam 1
Cassie: (from under the blanket) You're SMILING. At your PHONE. Somebody call 911, Alana's possessed.
@jump a_done
*a3
@add Discipline 2
Intervals go perfectly. You think about the text on every recovery jog. That part was not in the planner.
*a_done
@bg track_stadium_day
@show coachbrooks
Coach Brooks: Alana. Everyone keeps asking if we're related.
Alana: I know. I tell them we're not.
Coach Brooks: I tell them we are. It's funnier. (she hands you a coffee) Can I say something, as your coach?
Alana: Is it about my pacing?
Coach Brooks: It's about your face. You race like you're scared to lose control. Sometimes the best races happen when you stop holding the rope so tight.
> [Good] "Control is how I win." -> b1
> [Sweet] "...I don't know how to let go." -> b2
> [Bold] "Then watch me let go Saturday." -> b3
*b1
Coach Brooks: It is. Until it isn't. Think about it.
@jump b_done
*b2
@add Growth 3
Coach Brooks: (gently) Nobody does, at first. Start small. Say yes to one thing that isn't in the planner.
@jump b_done
*b3
@add Growth 2
@add Discipline 1
Coach Brooks: (raising her coffee) That's the most un-Alana thing I've ever heard. I love it.
*b_done
@bg dorm_room_night
That night you open your planner. You find a highlighter you've never used. Pink.
> [Sweet] Write "coffee w/ Cam" on Saturday. In pink. -> c1
> [Good] Write "rest day" in pink. Something just for you. -> c2
> [Bold] Throw the planner across the room. Just once. -> c3
*c1
@add Alana_Cam 3
It looks wrong on the page. Pink in a sea of blue. You leave it there anyway.
@jump end
*c2
@add Growth 2
Cassie: (peeking) Is that... a rest day? Voluntary? I'm calling your mom.
@jump end
*c3
@add Growth 3
It hits the wall. Cassie gasps. You both stare at it. Then you start laughing and can't stop. You pick it back up. You don't put it back in order.
*end
Alana Brooks has always run at 10K pace: steady, careful, perfect. This year she's learning that some things are worth a sprint.
